{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":504313,"name":"Leyla","username":"BigFluffyCookie","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/b/ce73a5/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-30T21:20:03.379Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eI want to use more of the connector apps on grok bot but a lot of them request write access in the OAuth grant with no way to configure the scope.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFrom what I understand after that grant, a write is not stopped by any fixed in-code rule but rather “Auto Review” checks the action before it runs. In the docs it says its an independent review model so whether a write stops for approval depends on that models decision.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI would like two controls for the connectors:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eLet me cap the OAuth scope, read-only should be the default with write, send, delete, etc.. being off unless I opt in.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eI want the capability to enable a “fixed check” , where for each mutating call ( POST / PUT / PATCH / DELETE ) I am guaranteed to get an approval card. This check should happen in code and the review model should not have any choice in this decision. This means I might get an approval card for some harmless post calls but I much prefer this over a write request going through without me allowing it first.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI think Auto Review is useful but I would like to have more controls on top of it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMentioned docs: \u003ca href=\"https://docs.x.ai/grok-bot/security#approvals-and-auto-review\" class=\"inline-onebox\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eGrok Bot security | SpaceXAI Docs\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":1,"updated_at":"2026-09-30T21:22:18.889Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":5,"reads":1,"readers_count":0,"score":25.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":173450,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-tighter-